{"uid":"e969704da14f50ed","name":"test_collapse_index_resolves_the_seed_flag_in_o1_bytes_regardless_of_setter_depth","fullName":"tests.test_log_merge_bounded_reads#test_collapse_index_resolves_the_seed_flag_in_o1_bytes_regardless_of_setter_depth","historyId":"23a39185f92cbc6c83a66c1fcae75bfe","time":{"start":1791916041577,"stop":1791916051930,"duration":10353},"description":"Task 021, PRD G.3/G.6: with a validated `collapse_index` present,\n    `merge_entries_tail` resolves the `textSeen`/`thinkingSeen` seed by\n    ONE lookup (`collapse_index.resolve_flags_at_offset`'s `bisect` over\n    the index's own segments) instead of `_tail_lines_of_file`'s bounded\n    LOOK-BACK GROWTH -- so the `output.jsonl` bytes actually read to\n    answer a `tail=2` request stay the SAME however far back the\n    deciding setter (the `text_delta`/`thinking_start` pair) sits, rather\n    than growing with that distance the way a re-reading growth ladder\n    would.\n\n    `prelude_count` (`_write_iteration_with_recognized_nonrendering_gap`,\n    `gap_count=0` so nothing else sits between the setter and the final\n    replaying `message_end`) places the setter 1,067 * `prelude_count`\n    bytes into the file -- 2,134,000 bytes at the smaller depth checked\n    here, 250x that (533,500,000 bytes) at the larger one -- and both\n    reads measure the exact same `_TAIL_READ_CHUNK` (65,536 bytes): the\n    ONE backward chunk `_tail_lines_of_file`'s ordinary `needed`-bounded\n    read always takes for a 2-line tail, with no extra growth at all\n    (`skip_seed_lookback=True`, since a valid index exists), and no\n    second read of any kind for the flags themselves -- those come from\n    the index file, never from `out`.\n\n    Byte-boundedness alone is not the property: a policy that stayed\n    cheap by DISCLOSING the flag unresolved (the shipped fallback this\n    same module already ships, PRD Q.1) would also read a constant\n    number of bytes here, and still answer wrong. So this also pins the\n    resolved seed itself, at both depths: no `unresolved` key, and both\n    `textSeen`/`thinkingSeen` measured `True` -- the setter really was\n    found, in O(1) work, not merely given up on cheaply.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 021, PRD G.3/G.6: with a validated <code>collapse_index</code> present,<br />\n<code>merge_entries_tail</code> resolves the <code>textSeen</code>/<code>thinkingSeen</code> seed by<br />\nONE lookup (<code>collapse_index.resolve_flags_at_offset</code>'s <code>bisect</code> over<br />\nthe index's own segments) instead of <code>_tail_lines_of_file</code>'s bounded<br />\nLOOK-BACK GROWTH -- so the <code>output.jsonl</code> bytes actually read to<br />\nanswer a <code>tail=2</code> request stay the SAME however far back the<br />\ndeciding setter (the <code>text_delta</code>/<code>thinking_start</code> pair) sits, rather<br />\nthan growing with that distance the way a re-reading growth ladder<br />\nwould.</p>\n<pre><code>`prelude_count` (`_write_iteration_with_recognized_nonrendering_gap`,\n`gap_count=0` so nothing else sits between the setter and the final\nreplaying `message_end`) places the setter 1,067 * `prelude_count`\nbytes into the file -- 2,134,000 bytes at the smaller depth checked\nhere, 250x that (533,500,000 bytes) at the larger one -- and both\nreads measure the exact same `_TAIL_READ_CHUNK` (65,536 bytes): the\nONE backward chunk `_tail_lines_of_file`'s ordinary `needed`-bounded\nread always takes for a 2-line tail, with no extra growth at all\n(`skip_seed_lookback=True`, since a valid index exists), and no\nsecond read of any kind for the flags themselves -- those come from\nthe index file, never from `out`.\n\nByte-boundedness alone is not the property: a policy that stayed\ncheap by DISCLOSING the flag unresolved (the shipped fallback this\nsame module already ships, PRD Q.1) would also read a constant\nnumber of bytes here, and still answer wrong. So this also pins the\nresolved seed itself, at both depths: no `unresolved` key, and both\n`textSeen`/`thinkingSeen` measured `True` -- the setter really was\nfound, in O(1) work, not merely given up on cheaply.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791915518597,"stop":1791915518597,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791915518598,"stop":1791915518598,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791916041541,"stop":1791916041552,"duration":11},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791916041541,"stop":1791916041541,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791916041552,"stop":1791916041552,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791916041553,"stop":1791916041561,"duration":8},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_undo_instant_sleep_patches","time":{"start":1791916041562,"stop